      "english": "And Saint John, the virgin, answered and spake [unto Him], saying, 'My Lord and my God, Who hast sanctified me unto Thyself, Who hast made all my thoughts to cling unto Thee, Who didst guard me and didst not permit me to take unto myself a wife; when Thou shalt gather all Thy clay into the Vally of Jehosaphat, in order that each one may receive according to what he hath done, whether it be good or whether it be evil, if Abbaton, the Angel of Death, shall come on that day, being in forms of his own person,--if this be so, I say, my Lord, there is not one soul that shall be able to stand before Thy awful throne.",
      "source": "Discourse on Abbaton, part 2",
      "urn": "urn:cts:copticLit:timothy.discourses.on_abbaton:22-54",
      "dialect": "sahidic"
    },
    {
      "coptic": "ⲉϣϫⲉⲁⲡⲛⲟⲩⲧⲉ ⲕⲁⲧⲁⲝⲓⲟⲩ ⲙⲙⲟϥ · ⲁϥⲉⲓ ⲉⲡⲉⲥⲏⲧ ⲉⲡⲕⲟⲥⲙⲟⲥ · ⲁϥϣⲁϫⲉ ⲙⲛⲡⲉϥ**ⲡⲗⲁⲥⲙⲁ** ⲉⲧⲃⲉⲡⲧⲁϩⲟ ⲉⲣⲁⲧϥ · ⲙⲡⲟⲩϫⲁⲓ ⲛⲧⲉⲩⲯⲩⲭⲏ ⲡⲟⲥⲟ ⲙⲁⲗⲗⲟⲛ ⲛϥⲛⲁⲧⲛⲛⲟⲟⲩ ⲁⲛ · ⲛⲛⲉϥⲡⲉⲧⲟⲩⲁⲁⲃ ⲛϥⲥⲗⲥⲱⲗⲟⲩ ϩⲛⲛⲉⲩϩⲓⲥⲉ ·",
